From: ipad-linux J407 bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: apple: support explicit hardware IRQ groups

Apple GPIO controllers expose up to seven hardware interrupt groups. The
current driver assumes that the N parent interrupts listed in DT correspond to
hardware groups 0..N-1, and assigns newly requested GPIO interrupts to group 0.

That assumption does not hold for every Apple GPIO instance. J407's AOP GPIO
controllers advertise only groups 4, 5 and 6 while using the same register
layout and apple,t8103-pinctrl compatible supported by the existing driver.

Add an optional apple,irq-groups property whose entries map each listed parent
interrupt to its hardware group number. Preserve the existing 0..N-1 mapping
when the property is absent. Assign newly started GPIO interrupts to the first
available hardware group instead of hard-coding group 0.

This is intentionally generic and keeps existing device trees behaviorally
unchanged.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml | 12 ++++++++++++
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c                          | 15 ++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
@@ -64,6 +64,18 @@ properties:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 7
 
+  apple,irq-groups:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 7
+    items:
+      minimum: 0
+      maximum: 6
+    description:
+      Hardware interrupt group corresponding to each entry in interrupts.
+      If absent, groups are assigned sequentially starting at zero, matching
+      the behavior expected by existing Apple device trees.
+
   interrupt-controller: true
 
   '#interrupt-cells':
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
@@ -270,9 +270,10 @@ static unsigned int apple_gpio_irq_startup(struct irq_data *data)
 {
 	struct gpio_chip *chip = irq_data_get_irq_chip_data(data);
 	struct apple_gpio_pinctrl *pctl = gpiochip_get_data(chip);
+	u8 irqgrp = pctl->irqgrps[0];
 
 	apple_gpio_set_reg(pctl, data->hwirq, REG_GPIOx_GRP,
-			   FIELD_PREP(REG_GPIOx_GRP, 0));
+			   FIELD_PREP(REG_GPIOx_GRP, irqgrp));
 
 	apple_gpio_direction_input(chip, data->hwirq);
 	apple_gpio_irq_unmask(data);
@@ -379,6 +380,7 @@ static int apple_gpio_register(struct apple_gpio_pinctrl *pctl)
 	if (girq->num_parents) {
 		int i;
+		u32 irqgrp;
 
 		gpio_irq_chip_set_chip(girq, &apple_gpio_irqchip);
 		girq->parent_handler = apple_gpio_irq_handler;
@@ -397,7 +399,14 @@ static int apple_gpio_register(struct apple_gpio_pinctrl *pctl)
 				goto out_free_irq_data;
 
 			girq->parents[i] = ret;
-			pctl->irqgrps[i] = i;
+
+			ret = of_property_read_u32_index(pctl->dev->of_node,
+							 "apple,irq-groups", i, &irqgrp);
+			if (ret == -EINVAL)
+				irqgrp = i;
+			else if (ret || irqgrp > FIELD_MAX(REG_GPIOx_GRP))
+				goto out_free_irq_data;
+
+			pctl->irqgrps[i] = irqgrp;
 			irq_data[i] = &pctl->irqgrps[i];
 		}
 
-- 
